{"resourceIdentifier":"1672","resourceName":"Musokotwane REDD+ Project","description":"The project area is located in Kazungula district, Zambia. The soils of the project area are quite variable in composition depending on the physiographic position. The project area experiences tropical climate in which summers are hot and wet. Subsistence farming is the mainstay for most of the population in the project district. The Musokotwane REDD+ project comprises diverse vegetation formation and ecosystems ranging from lush tropical grasslands, Acacia woodlands, Kalahari woodlands, and Miombo forests. These forest ecosystems are a host to globally unique and diverse fauna and flora. The combined forest area under the Musokotwane REDD+ project area is approximately 165,000 ha of which Teak forests is 15,000 ha, Miombo woodlands 85,000 ha and Mopane woodlands 65,000 ha. The total standing biomass in these forests stand at 75,923,780 tones. Therefore, the implementation of the project activities will prevent the emission of 33,891,146.52 tCO2e over the 30 years project duration.","location":{"latitude":-17.566389,"longitude":25.732770},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1672"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Kazungula District"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Zambruss Enterprises"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Withdrawn"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1100000"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"REDD"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VM0009"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string",